+Scope-owned cancellation (benchmark extension v1)
+------------------------------------------------
+
+The ``sf004-cancellation-ownership-v1`` task extends the asyncio backend's
+cooperative cancellation contract. This section describes the benchmark
+extension, not a released upstream version.
+
+A cancellation raised by ``from_thread.check_cancelled()`` belongs to the scope
+responsible for it. A separately cancelled sibling or shielded child scope must
+not swallow that cancellation. Neither a saved exception from a finished
+operation nor an ordinary ``asyncio.CancelledError`` with similar text becomes
+the cancellation of a new scope. The first reason passed to the responsible
+scope's ``cancel()`` remains visible to the worker.
+
+Existing level cancellation still applies: when a cancelled child scope must
+propagate its cancellation to a visible cancelled ancestor during scope exit,
+the ancestor can take responsibility. A shield prevents that handoff.
+Unrelated cancellation leaves must not be relabelled during the transfer.
+
+Ownership and exception context are preserved through nested worker/coroutine
+round trips and framework cancellation wrappers. In a nested exception group,
+only owned cancellation leaves are consumed; foreign cancellations and ordinary
+errors remain in their original order and remaining group structure.
+
+Worker reuse does not transfer cancellation state to a fresh operation.
+Concurrent worker operations keep separate scope associations, and worker
+cancellation checks continue to respect the current shield state.
